# The gimbal's rangefinder, added to SITL's defaults when the robot has one
# (ROBOT_RANGEFINDER, with ROBOT_GIMBAL). sim-agent's model has a single-point
# laser rangefinder along the camera's axis, which the ArduPilotPlugin sends as
# rng_1; type 100 reads it, and it reaches MAVLink as DISTANCE_SENSOR id 0.
#
# ArduPilot only puts a rangefinder on MAVLink as an RNGFND, which it takes
# to be fixed to the airframe. A mount driver's rangefinder (Siyi, Topotek,
# Viewpro) goes to the log and Lua only. So where it points comes from the
# gimbal's attitude (GIMBAL_DEVICE_ATTITUDE_STATUS), not from the message.

RNGFND1_TYPE     100
# DISTANCE_SENSOR carries centimetres in a uint16, so 655 m at most. The
# sensor in rangefinder.sdf reaches as far, and nearer than MIN, so a close
# target is out of range low here.
RNGFND1_MIN      0.2
RNGFND1_MAX      650

# It turns with the gimbal, so it isn't the downward rangefinder (25) Copter
# would take as height above ground: flight code, surface tracking and the
# EKF only read that one. Forward (0) is only read by collision avoidance,
# and only through the proximity RangeFinder driver (PRXn_TYPE 4), which is
# off here. Never turn that on with a gimbal rangefinder: avoidance would
# take whatever the gimbal looks at for an obstacle dead ahead. QGC draws
# the reading as an arc ahead of the vehicle too, for the same reason.
RNGFND1_ORIENT   0

# A camera's rangefinder doesn't decide whether the drone can fly: skip the
# rangefinder arming check (bit 15).
ARMING_SKIPCHK   32768
